what time scale and how to
glue them back together.

00:19:47.011 --> 00:19:50.150
So, it's not just
allocating the resources,

00:19:50.151 --> 00:19:53.090
but also allocating
the functions.

00:19:53.091 --> 00:19:56.800
How each function is
carried out it is less of

00:19:56.801 --> 00:20:01.220
a concern for
the decomposition itself.

00:20:01.221 --> 00:20:05.830
Now, there is the vertical
decomposition layering as

00:20:05.831 --> 00:20:08.815
a fundamental concept
in networking to

00:20:08.816 --> 00:20:12.080
modularize a complex
interacting system.

00:20:12.081 --> 00:20:14.390
Layering can be mathematically

00:20:14.391 --> 00:20:17.495
understood as optimisation
decompensation,

00:20:17.496 --> 00:20:19.320
both reverse engineering and

00:20:19.321 --> 00:20:22.790
also a design synthesis
for engineering.

00:20:22.791 --> 00:20:25.735
For example, Kumar
was the one who gave

00:20:25.736 --> 00:20:28.680
me and many in the community
a lot of inspiration back.

00:20:28.681 --> 00:20:31.760
This is 15 plus years ago also

00:20:31.761 --> 00:20:33.760
on the notion of

00:20:33.761 --> 00:20:36.850
architecture and thinking
about layering that way.

00:20:36.851 --> 00:20:39.870
Now, this subject that
Victor is putting together,

00:20:39.871 --> 00:20:43.540
the panel this morning
on Intelligent edge now,

00:20:43.541 --> 00:20:45.070
I think of the Cloud and

00:20:45.071 --> 00:20:49.920
Edge/Fog as a horizontal
decomposition.

00:20:49.921 --> 00:20:52.870
All the architectures
in some sense

00:20:52.871 --> 00:20:55.360
are there to be a little

00:20:55.361 --> 00:20:58.100
philosophical if
you will and then

00:20:58.101 --> 00:21:01.195
to support a range of
practical applications.

00:21:01.196 --> 00:21:03.635
For example, in 1948,

00:21:03.636 --> 00:21:06.340
the Shannon Source-Channel
Separation is

00:21:06.341 --> 00:21:09.165
an architectural principle and

00:21:09.166 --> 00:21:12.700
very crisply stated
mathematically as well,

00:21:12.701 --> 00:21:16.360
and that principle
in architecture

00:21:16.361 --> 00:21:18.540
further led to the applications

00:21:18.541 --> 00:21:20.520
of digital communications.

00:21:20.521 --> 00:21:24.655
When Sir Bob Kahn did
the TCP/IP published in

00:21:24.656 --> 00:21:29.180
74 and that is
an architectural design,

00:21:29.181 --> 00:21:32.445
and that led to
the vertical applications

00:21:32.446 --> 00:21:34.440
in the Internet and the web.

00:21:34.441 --> 00:21:36.630
Then the Edge and Fog,

00:21:36.631 --> 00:21:40.080
my biggest hope is
that it will continue

00:21:40.081 --> 00:21:43.120
to be worked on by the community

00:21:43.121 --> 00:21:45.560
from industry and
academia around the world

00:21:45.561 --> 00:21:48.760
and arise these
architectural foundations

00:21:48.761 --> 00:21:55.280
for applications such as IoT
and 5G or Dispersive AIs.

