the forage varieties,

01:21:14.121 --> 01:21:15.470
so I can actually talk at length.

01:21:15.471 --> 01:21:16.780
Maybe later on, we can do that.

01:21:16.781 --> 01:21:19.060
But just to talk
about it quickly,

01:21:19.061 --> 01:21:21.085
there is trust that
is in the Cloud,

01:21:21.086 --> 01:21:22.440
which obviously you trust more

01:21:22.441 --> 01:21:25.220
because we make sure
that it is trusted.

01:21:25.221 --> 01:21:26.890
What we do is, we try to

01:21:26.891 --> 01:21:28.795
take the trust and
bring it to the device.

01:21:28.796 --> 01:21:31.735
How we do it, is through device
identity and attestation.

01:21:31.736 --> 01:21:34.560
We identify the device
through hardware means,

01:21:34.561 --> 01:21:36.340
so TPM and such,

01:21:36.341 --> 01:21:38.930
and then we build trust
with attestation of

01:21:38.931 --> 01:21:41.565
firmware and software
that runs on top of it.

01:21:41.566 --> 01:21:44.675
This part of it is not
only Microsoft doing it,

01:21:44.676 --> 01:21:46.895
we have to have Silicon firmware,

01:21:46.896 --> 01:21:49.685
manufacturers, OEMs,
who contribute to it.

01:21:49.686 --> 01:21:52.105
To enable that, we have
a certification program.

01:21:52.106 --> 01:21:54.950
So, we certify IoT Edge devices,

01:21:54.951 --> 01:21:58.560
which conform to this whole
building of trust mechanism.

01:21:58.561 --> 01:22:00.145
So, it's not any device.

01:22:00.146 --> 01:22:02.050
If you want to be really secure,

01:22:02.051 --> 01:22:05.340
you go and get the certified
device to do that.

